{
  "id": "u03-l03",
  "unit": "u03-family",
  "title": "Father's side",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "English has one 'uncle'; Bengali has a different word for each one! On your **father's side**:\n\n- **দাদা / দাদি** — grandfather / grandmother\n- **চাচা / চাচি** — father's brother / his wife\n- **ফুফু / ফুফা** — father's sister / her husband\n\nTo say 'father's', add **-র**: বাবা → **বাবার**. So **চাচা আমার বাবার ভাই** = 'Chacha is my father's brother.'\n\n**Watch out — Kolkata difference:** in Bangladesh **দাদা** is your *grandfather*, but in Kolkata (and many Hindu families in Bangladesh) দাদা means *elder brother*! There, paternal grandparents are ঠাকুরদা / ঠাকুমা, father's brother is কাকা, and father's sister is পিসি.",
